    "title": "Snippets from a Master Gardener - Like-Minded Plant People - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By kylelpj ,\n19 hours ago I know why I wanted to be a “Master Gardener”. I had just moved to Ruston from a very different dry climate in the high elevation desert in Reno, Nevada. Due to the threat of late frosts there, it is a huge risk to plant before Mother’s Day and is usually safe to plant by Memorial Day. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
